+++++++++++++++++++++++++
How to navigate this repo:
+++++++++++++++++++++++++

++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Run in this order, this will generate relevant files, which should save to project_data folder ->
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

demand_estimate_generation.ipynb
    generates: demand_estimate.csv
                    - estimates of demand using assumed norm dist and taking the 95th interval
                    - saved to project_data
route_generation.py
    generates: feasible_routes.csv
                    - table of all feasible routes. generated using nearest neighbor method.
                    - saved to project_data
mixed_integer_program.py ---> for this enter 'C' on keyboard when prompted to run cost reduction specifically
    generates: Optimal_Routes.csv
                Renamed files in repo: Optimal_Routes_Cost.csv
                                       Optimal_Routes_Fuel.csv
                    - table with the combination of routes that is optimal
                    - saved to project_data
               MIP_Summary.csv
                    - table with the summary data for quick reference
scheduling.py
    generates: Scheduled_Optimal_Routes.csv
                    - this is purely used for generating maps and sanity checking that the optimal
                    routes that have been generated can actually be implemented in the real world
                    - saved to project_data
mapping.ipynb
    generates: Optimal_Routes_Weekdays_8AM.html
               Optimal_Routes_Weekdays_2PM.html
               Optimal_Routes_Saturdays_8AM.html
               Optimal_Routes_Saturdays_2PM.html
                    - maps in html format for each shift Weekdays and Saturdays, can be screenshotted
                    - saved to project_data/maps

++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Individual simulations in no particular order:
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

TRAFFIC SIMULATION:
New_traffic_simulation.py
    generates: output simulation data ONLY for traffic
 -> simulation_traffic_visualisations.py

simulation_traffic.py
    - old simulation that does NOT output the correct data

DEMAND SIMULATION:
simulation_demand.py
    generates: simulation_demand_results.csv
               simulation_demand_summary.csv
                    - bootstraps all the raw demand values and sends it through route gen and LP.
                    Then plots the data using the visualisation file.
                    - This is ONLY simulation on demand
 -> simulation_demand_visualisations.ipynb

COMBINED SIM (USE THIS):
combined_demand_traffic_sim.ipynb
    generates: visualisations within the notebook as well as a paired ttest
                    - uses Monte Carlo simulation structure, bootstrap for demand, lognormal multipliers for traffic
                    - both get applied

PAIRED T-TESTS:
paired_ttest_fuel_base.ipynb
    generates: paired t-test and visualisations in the notebook
                    - uses Monte Carlo simulation structure, bootstrap for demand, lognormal multipliers for traffic
                    - applies this to fuel data in Optimal_Routes_Cost.csv and Optimal_Routes_Fuel.csv
                    - a paired ttest is then applied

paired_traffic_no_traffic_ttest.ipynb
    generates: t-test comparing traffic vs. no traffic conditions

OTHER VISUALIZATIONS & ASSETS:
cost_and_demand_visualizations.py
    - script used to plot cost and demand figures

weekly_pallet_demand_vs_lp_baseline.png
    - generated plot comparing weekly pallet demand against the LP baseline